e peoples</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Mande peoples are a family of ethnic groups of West Africa who speak Mande languages, among them the Malinke, Bambara, Soninke, Dyula and Mende.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mandelieu-la-napoule"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mandelieu-la-napoule.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Mandelieu-la-Napoule</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Mandelieu-la-Napoule is a town on the French Riviera in the Alpes-Maritimes department, just west of Cannes at the mouth of the Siagne.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/manding"><span class="enc-name">Manding</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Manding, or Manden, is the historical heartland of the Mandinka people on the upper Niger, on the border of modern Mali and Guinea, around Kangaba and Niani.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mandinka"><span class="enc-name">Mandinka</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Mandinka are a West African people of the Mande group, living mainly in present-day Mali, Guinea, Senegal and the Gambia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mandla"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mandla.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Mandla</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Mandla is a town on the Narmada river in Madhya Pradesh, India, and the headquarters of Mandla district.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mandonius"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mandonius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Mandonius</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Mandonius was a chief of the Ilergetes, an Iberian people of north-eastern Spain, who led them with his brother Indibilis during the Second Punic War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mandor-affair"><span class="enc-name">Mandor affair</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The Mandor affair was a series of mass killings carried out by the Japanese occupation forces in West Kalimantan in 1943 and 1944.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mandore"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mandore.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Mandore</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Mandore, anciently Mandavyapura, is a historic town a few kilometres north of Jodhpur in Rajasthan, India.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mandsaur"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mandsaur.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Mandsaur</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Mandsaur is a city in the Malwa region of western Madhya Pradesh, India.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mandu"><span class="enc-name">Mandu</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Mandu is a ruined fortress city on a plateau of the Vindhya range in Madhya Pradesh, India.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mandubracius"><span class="enc-name">Mandubracius</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Mandubracius was a prince of the Trinovantes in south-eastern Britain whose father had been killed by Cassivellaunus.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mandume-ya-ndemufayo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mandume-ya-ndemufayo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Mandume ya Ndemufayo</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Mandume ya Ndemufayo was the last independent king of the Kwanyama, an Ovambo people living across the border of southern Angola and northern Namibia, reigning from 1911.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/manduria"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/manduria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Manduria</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Manduria is a town in the province of Taranto in Apulia, southern Italy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mandvi-kutch"><span class="enc-name">Mandvi, Kutch</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Mandvi is a port town in the Kutch district of Gujarat, India, on the Gulf of Kutch at the mouth of the Rukmavati river.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/manendragarh"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/manendragarh.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Manendragarh</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Manendragarh is a town in northern Chhattisgarh, India, near the border with Madhya Pradesh, in the area of the former princely state of Korea, or Koriya.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/manetho"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/manetho.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Manetho</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Manetho was an Egyptian priest of Sebennytos in the Nile Delta who wrote a history of Egypt in Greek, the Aegyptiaca, under the early Ptolemies in the 3rd century BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/manfred-king-of-sicily"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/manfred-king-of-sicily.jpg" alt="" loading="laz